cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use SECA in your research, please cite it as below."

title: "SECA: Stellar Evolutionary Classification with Asteroseismology"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Figueira"
    given-names: "Pedro"

version: "1.0.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/pedrorfigueira/seca"

license: "MIT"

abstract: >
  SECA (Stellar Evolutionary Classification with Asteroseismology) is a
  Python package for classifying stars into broad evolutionary stages from
  their stellar mass, radius, and effective temperature using standard
  asteroseismic scaling relations and mass-dependent calibrations based on
  stellar evolutionary models.

keywords:
  - stellar evolution
  - asteroseismology
  - stellar classification
  - Gaia
  - exoplanets
